sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Acanthometra pellucida Schnakenberg wavelength at 206 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Acanthometra pellucida morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Acanthometra pellucida specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/acanthometra_pellucida_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Acanthometra pellucida; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) reaction-diffusion and a critical wavelength; Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) activator-inhibitor kinetics; Murray (1981) the critical-wavenumber formula used for prepatterns. | Haeckel (1904) Kunstformen der Natur, Tafel 21, is a published drawing captioned Acanthometra. | Decelle et al. (2012) describe living acantharians. They do not report a 206 nm pigment period.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.14, 0.76), k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv), and a six-point gamma sweep on a periodic 96x96 patch. | Equal-diffusion ablation. Spine-axis angles measured on the vendored plate crop.; transfer_boundary: 206 nm (2.064e-7 m, log10 -6.685) is the assigned detail scale. The length unit is chosen so the analytical wavelength equals that number. The plate's scale is the printed drawing, not 206 nm. | Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. There is no fossil predecessor in this slot. The comparison is with a 412 nm octave on a 1339 nm patch (6 waves versus 3).; does_not_claim: That celestite spicules of A. pellucida have been shown to form by this Schnakenberg system. | That Tafel 21 figure 2 is a photograph of the type of A. pellucida. | That the plate resolves a 206 nm carrier.]; other sources: Kunstformen der Natur, Tafel 21 <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acanthometra._-_Stachelstrahlinge_LCCN2015648908.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 223 nm (2.232e-07 m, log10=-6.651 m, tier=2_macromolecular_100nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 223 nm to 653 µm): 223 nm:acanthometra-pellucida-bioelectric-polarity, 802 nm:acanthometra-pellucida-vertex-packing, 15 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength, 27 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-clock-wavefront, 46 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-morphogen-condensation, 59 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-flux-canalization, 66 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-elastic-buckling, 76 µm:acanthometra-pellucida-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1212303109>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-acanthometra-pellucida-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

